  "source_findings": [
    "lua.c lua_readline delegates presentation/input to a loaded or linked readline backend; its fallback writes the prompt then fgets without echo.",
    "luaconf.h selects dynamic libreadline.so on Linux and linked LUA_USE_READLINE on macOS. The oracle preserves these native platform definitions.",
    "testes/main.lua uses presence/pattern checks for prompts and line-substring checks for interactive results. The supplemental exact prompt-only expectation came from the Windows/fgets configuration.",
    "Ada CLI Read_Line currently implements the fgets-like path. External line editing and actual terminal behavior remain a separate implementation/acceptance question."
  ],
  "next_required_evidence": [
    "Collect all 19 native prompt contracts and two setup probes on Linux/macOS without stopping at the first mismatch; preserve each contract error and raw process identity.",
    "Independently decide a bounded backend-specific native counterpart protocol that retains Lua side effects, prompt values/callback order, errors and statuses. No status-only approval or raw-output normalization.",
    "Keep native T no-close observations outside the Windows-only diagnostic authority until source-linked same-context applicability has independent review.",
    "Fresh strict full-context captures and final acceptance remain required after implementation and reviews."
